#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><tip><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:267
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You should consider installing some sort of password checking dictionary so "
"that you can configure the installation to only accept strong passwords. A "
"suitable dictionary to use is shown in the <xref linkend=\"cracklib\"/> "
"instructions. Note that only one file can be used, but you can concatenate "
"many files into one. The configuration file shown below assumes you have "
"installed a dictionary to <filename>/usr/share/dict/words</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Você deveria considerar instalar algum tipo de dicionário de verificação de "
"senha, de forma que consiga configurar a instalação para aceitar somente "
"senhas fortes. Um dicionário adequado para usar é mostrado nas instruções do"
" <xref linkend=\"cracklib\"/>. Observe que somente um arquivo pode ser "
"usado, mas você pode concatenar muitos arquivos em um. O arquivo de "
"configuração mostrado abaixo assume que você tenha instalado um dicionário "
"em <filename>/usr/share/dict/words</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:278
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create the Kerberos configuration file with the following commands issued by"
" the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Crie o arquivo de configuração do Kerberos com os seguintes comandos "
"emitidos pelo(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:283
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/krb5.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/krb5.conf\n"
"\n"
"[libdefaults]\n"
"    default_realm = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"    encrypt = true\n"
"\n"
"[realms]\n"
"    <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable> = {\n"
"        kdc = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        admin_server = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        dict_file = /usr/share/dict/words\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"[domain_realm]\n"
"    .<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable> = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"[logging]\n"
"    kdc = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    admin_server = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    default = SYSLOG:DEBUG:DAEMON\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/krb5.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/krb5.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Início /etc/krb5.conf\n"
"\n"
"[libdefaults]\n"
"    default_realm = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"    encrypt = true\n"
"\n"
"[realms]\n"
"    <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable> = {\n"
"        kdc = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        admin_server = <replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"        dict_file = /usr/share/dict/words\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"[domain_realm]\n"
"    .<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable> = <replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"[logging]\n"
"    kdc = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    admin_server = SYSLOG:INFO:AUTH\n"
"    default = SYSLOG:DEBUG:DAEMON\n"
"\n"
"# Fim /etc/krb5.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:309
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You will need to substitute your domain and proper hostname for the "
"occurrences of the <replaceable>&lt;belgarath&gt;</replaceable> and "
"<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable> names."
msgstr ""
"Você precisará substituir seu domínio e nome adequado do dispositivo para as"
" ocorrências dos nomes <replaceable>&lt;belgarath&gt;</replaceable> e "
"<replaceable>&lt;example.org&gt;</replaceable>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:315
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>default_realm</option> should be the name of your domain changed to "
"ALL CAPS. This isn't required, but both <application>Heimdal</application> "
"and MIT recommend it."
msgstr ""
"<option>default_realm</option> deveria ser o nome do seu domínio mudado para"
" TUDO EM MAIÚSCULAS. Isso não é obrigatório, mas tanto o "
"<application>Heimdal</application> quanto o MIT o recomendam."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:321
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>encrypt = true</option> provides encryption of all traffic between "
"kerberized clients and servers. It's not necessary and can be left off. If "
"you leave it off, you can encrypt all traffic from the client to the server "
"using a switch on the client program instead."
msgstr ""
"<option>encrypt = true</option> fornece encriptação de todo o tráfego entre "
"clientes e servidores kerberizados. Não é necessário e pode ser deixado de "
"lado. Se você deixá-lo desativado, [então] consegue encriptar todo o tráfego"
" procedente do cliente para o servidor usando uma chave no aplicativo "
"cliente."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:329
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <option>[realms]</option> parameters tell the client programs where to "
"look for the KDC authentication services."
msgstr ""
"Os parâmetros <option>[realms]</option> dizem aos aplicativos clientes onde "
"procurar pelos serviços de autenticação do KDC."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:334
#, xml-text
msgid "The <option>[domain_realm]</option> section maps a domain to a realm."
msgstr ""
"A seção <option>[domain_realm]</option> mapeia um domínio para um reino."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:338
#, xml-text
msgid "Create the KDC database:"
msgstr "Crie a base de dados do KDC:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:341
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kdb5_util create -r "
"<replaceable>&lt;EXAMPLE.ORG&gt;</replaceable> -s</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>kdb5_util create -r "
"<replaceable>&lt;EXEMPLO.ORG&gt;</replaceable> -s</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:344
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now you should populate the database with principals (users). For now, just "
"use your regular login name or <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>."
msgstr ""
"Agora você deveria povoar a base de dados com principais (usuários(as)). Por"
" enquanto, apenas use seu nome normal de login ou <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:349
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kadmin.local\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> add_policy dict-only\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -policy dict-only <replaceable>&lt;loginname&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>kadmin.local\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> add_policy dict-only\n"
"<prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -policy dict-only <replaceable>&lt;nome_login&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:354
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The KDC server and any machine running kerberized server daemons must have a"
" host key installed:"
msgstr ""
"O servidor KDC e qualquer máquina executando processos de segundo plano de "
"servidor kerberizados precisam ter uma chave de dispositivo instalada:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:358
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -randkey "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> addprinc -randkey "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.exemplo.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:361
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"After choosing the defaults when prompted, you will have to export the data "
"to a keytab file:"
msgstr ""
"Depois de escolher os padrões quando solicitado, você terá que exportar os "
"dados para um arquivo de tabela de chave:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:365
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> ktadd "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.example.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput><prompt>kadmin.local:</prompt> ktadd "
"host/<replaceable>&lt;belgarath.exemplo.org&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:368
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This should have created a file in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc</filename> named <filename>krb5.keytab</filename> "
"(Kerberos 5). This file should have 600 (<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> rw only)  permissions. Keeping the "
"keytab files from public access is crucial to the overall security of the "
"Kerberos installation."
msgstr ""
"Isso deveria ter criado um arquivo em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc</filename> chamado <filename>krb5.keytab</filename>"
" (Kerberos 5). Esse arquivo deveria ter permissões 600 (somente leitura e "
"escrita por <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>). Manter os "
"arquivos de tabela de chave do acesso público é crucial para a segurança "
"geral da instalação do Kerberos."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:377
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Exit the <command>kadmin</command> program (use <command>quit</command> or "
"<command>exit</command>) and return back to the shell prompt. Start the KDC "
"daemon manually, just to test out the installation:"
msgstr ""
"Saia do aplicativo <command>kadmin</command> (use <command>quit</command> ou"
" <command>exit</command>) e retorne ao prompt do shell. Inicie o processo de"
" segundo plano KDC manualmente, apenas para testar a instalação:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:383
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>/usr/sbin/krb5kdc</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>/usr/sbin/krb5kdc</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:386
#, xml-text
msgid "Attempt to get a ticket with the following command:"
msgstr "Tente obter um tíquete com o seguinte comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:389
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>kinit <replaceable>&lt;loginname&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>kinit <replaceable>&lt;nome_login&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:392
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You will be prompted for the password you created. After you get your "
"ticket, you can list it with the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Você será solicitado(a) a fornecer a senha que criou. Depois de obter seu "
"tíquete, você consegue listá-lo com o seguinte comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:396
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>klist</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>klist</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:399
#, xml-text
msgid "Information about the ticket should be displayed on the screen."
msgstr "Informação a respeito do tíquete deveriam ser exibidas na tela."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:404
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the functionality of the keytab file, issue the following command as"
" the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Para testar a funcionalidade do arquivo de tabela de chave, emita o seguinte"
" comando como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:409
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ktutil\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> rkt /etc/krb5.keytab\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> l</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ktutil\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> rkt /etc/krb5.keytab\n"
"<prompt>ktutil:</prompt> l</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:414
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This should dump a list of the host principal, along with the encryption "
"methods used to access the principal."
msgstr ""
"Isso deveria despejar uma lista do principal do dispositivo, juntamente com "
"os métodos de encriptação usados para acessar o principal."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:419
#, xml-text
msgid "Create an empty ACL file that can be modified later:"
msgstr "Crie um arquivo ACL vazio que possa ser modificado posteriormente:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:422
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>touch /var/lib/krb5kdc/kadm5.acl</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>touch /var/lib/krb5kdc/kadm5.acl</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:425
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At this point, if everything has been successful so far, you can feel fairly"
" confident in the installation and configuration of the package."
msgstr ""
"Neste ponto, se tudo deu certo até agora, [então] você pode se sentir "
"bastante confiante na instalação e configuração do pacote."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:433
#, xml-text
msgid "Additional Information"
msgstr "Informação Adicional"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:436
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For additional information consult the <ulink "
"url=\"https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/www/krb5-&mitkrb-major-"
"version;/#documentation\"> documentation for krb5-&mitkrb-version;</ulink> "
"on which the above instructions are based."
msgstr ""
"Para informação adicional, consulte a <ulink "
"url=\"https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/www/krb5-&mitkrb-major-"
"version;/#documentation\">documentação para krb5-&mitkrb-version;</ulink> na"
" qual as instruções acima são baseadas."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:447
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Init Script</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\">Systemd Unit</phrase>"
msgstr ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Script de Iniciação</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\">Unidade do Systemd</phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:451
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you want to start <application>Kerberos</application> services at boot, "
"install the <filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/krb5</filename> init script included "
"in the <xref linkend=\"bootscripts\"/> package using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Se você deseja iniciar os serviços <application>Kerberos</application> na "
"inicialização, [então] instale o script de iniciação "
"<filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/krb5</filename> incluído no pacote <xref "
"linkend=\"bootscripts\"/> usando o seguinte comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:458
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you want to start <application>Kerberos</application> services at boot, "
"install the <filename>krb5.service</filename> unit included in the <xref "
"linkend=\"systemd-units\"/> package using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Se você deseja iniciar os serviços <application>Kerberos</application> na "
"inicialização, [então] instale a unidade <filename>krb5.service</filename> "
"incluída no pacote <xref linkend=\"systemd-units\"/> usando o seguinte "
"comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:464
#, xml-text
msgid "krb5"
msgstr "krb5"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/mitkrb.xml:467
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-krb5</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>make install-krb5</userinput>"

